  "readme": [
    {
      "section": "dsh-models-usage（模型用量与余额）",
      "text": "[English](README.en.md)\n\nDeepSeek Harness 插件，汇总当前已配置的服务商和模型，并展示服务商账户余额或订阅额度。"
    },
    {
      "section": "功能",
      "text": "- 查看服务商、模型及上下文、输入类型等模型信息，并支持搜索和筛选。\n- 查询部分服务商的官方余额或额度；无法自动查询的服务商会明确标注，并提供控制台入口，不会以 0 代替未知余额。\n- 支持逐服务商刷新、额度重置时间和短期缓存。\n- 可通过卡片上的「自定义查询」配置其他余额或额度接口，测试并预览字段映射。配置只保存请求模板，不保存 API 密钥。\n\n余额与额度是**服务商账户级**信息，不按模型拆分。是否支持查询及所需凭据可在面板的「查看支持现状」中查看。"
    },
    {
      "section": "安装与使用",
      "text": "通过 CLI 安装：\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin add dsh-models-usage\n```\n\n也可以在 Harness 的 **Plugins → Add plugin** 中搜索或填写 `dsh-models-usage`，然后启用插件。\n\n启用后，从左侧打开「模型用量与余额」面板。面板需要一个活动会话；点击顶部刷新按钮可更新数据。也可在会话中使用：\n\n```text\n/dsh-models-usage [summary|detail|refresh] [provider=<id>]\n```\n\n`models_balance` 工具会返回同一份数据，供模型调用。"
    },
    {
      "section": "配置",
      "text": "在 `cordis.patch.yml` 的 `models-usage` 插件配置中可调整：\n\n| 选项 | 默认值 | 说明 |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `includeModelDetails` | `true` | 是否加载模型上下文、能力等详细信息 |\n| `includeDormantProviders` | `false` | 是否包含尚未配置或未激活的服务商 |\n| `locale` | `zh-CN` | 上报给余额接口的语言 |\n| `clientVersion` | `0.2.0-rc.2` | 上报给余额接口的客户端版本 |\n| `customQueryFile` | 空 | 自定义查询配置文件路径；默认是 `$DSH_HOME/storages/dsh-models-usage.custom-queries.json` |"
    },
    {
      "section": "开发",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install --legacy-peer-deps\nnpm run typecheck\nnpm run build\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "限制",
      "text": "- 面板通过当前活动会话与 Host 通信；没有活动会话时，请先打开一个会话。\n- 并非所有服务商都提供可用模型密钥访问的余额接口。插件不会使用控制台 Cookie 或把套餐额度折算成现金余额。\n- 余额是账户级数据，不能按单个模型拆分。"
    },
    {
      "section": "许可证",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    },
    {
      "section": "dsh-models-usage — Model Usage & Balances",
      "text": "[简体中文](README.md)\n\nA DeepSeek Harness plugin that brings configured providers and models together with each provider's account balance or plan quota."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "- Browse providers and models, including context limits and input capabilities; search and filter the list.\n- Query official balances or quotas for supported providers. Providers without an available query are clearly marked and linked to their console instead of showing a fabricated zero balance.\n- Refresh providers individually and view quota reset times, with short-lived caching.\n- Configure custom balance or quota queries from a provider card, then test the request and preview field mappings. Saved configurations contain request templates, not API keys."
    },
    {
      "section": "Features",
      "text": "Balances and quotas belong to the **provider account**, not individual models. Check **View support status** in the panel for current coverage and credential requirements."
    },
    {
      "section": "Install and use",
      "text": "Install with the CLI:\n\n```sh\ndsh plugin add dsh-models-usage\n```\n\nAlternatively, use **Plugins → Add plugin** in Harness to find or enter `dsh-models-usage`, then enable the plugin.\n\nOpen **Model Usage & Balances** from the sidebar. The panel requires an active conversation; use the refresh button to update the data. You can also run this command in a conversation:\n\n```text\n/dsh-models-usage [summary|detail|refresh] [provider=<id>]\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Install and use",
      "text": "The `models_balance` tool returns the same data for model use."
    },
    {
      "section": "Configuration",
      "text": "| Option | Default | Description |\n| --- | --- | --- |\n| `includeModelDetails` | `true` | Load per-model context and capability details |\n| `includeDormantProviders` | `false` | Include providers that are not configured or active |\n| `locale` | `zh-CN` | Locale sent to balance APIs |\n| `clientVersion` | `0.2.0-rc.2` | Client version sent to balance APIs |\n| `customQueryFile` | empty | Custom query configuration path; defaults to `$DSH_HOME/storages/dsh-models-usage.custom-queries.json` |"
    },
    {
      "section": "Development",
      "text": "```sh\nnpm install --legacy-peer-deps\nnpm run typecheck\nnpm run build\n```"
    },
    {
      "section": "Limitations",
      "text": "- The panel communicates with the Host through the active conversation. Open a conversation first if none is active.\n- Not every provider exposes a balance API accessible with a model API key. The plugin does not use console cookies or convert plan quotas into cash balances.\n- Balances are account-level data and cannot be split by model."
    },
    {
      "section": "License",
      "text": "[MIT](LICENSE)"
    }
  ],
